# Decimal remainder with float operands

Takes 10.5 modulo 1.5 in both operand orders to verify the f32 value
converts into a decimal remainder, producing 0.0 when the decimal is the
dividend and 1.5 when the float is the dividend.

>>> source
decimal_value: decimal = 10.5
float_divisor: float = 1.5
float_dividend: float = 10.5
decimal_divisor: decimal = 3

// Verifies the Decimal/Float conversion.
decimal_remainder: decimal = decimal_value % float_divisor
print(decimal_remainder)

// Verifies the same conversion with the operand order reversed.
float_remainder: decimal = float_dividend % decimal_divisor
print(float_remainder)

<<< stdout
0.0
1.5

<<< stderr
